From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 11:17:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: skip temperature reads for inactive pdevs

With a shared wiphy, the hardware can be running while an individual
pdev has no usable channels and did not complete MAC start. Its WMI
temperature response is ignored because the pdev is inactive, causing
the sysfs reader to wait for the five-second timeout.

Check the active pdev table under the existing wiphy lock before
sending the request. Leave temperature reads for active radios intact.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/thermal.c
@@ -153,7 +153,8 @@
 
 	guard(wiphy)(ath12k_ar_to_hw(ar)->wiphy);
 
-	if (ar->ah->state != ATH12K_HW_STATE_ON)
+	if (ar->ah->state != ATH12K_HW_STATE_ON ||
+	    !rcu_access_pointer(ar->ab->pdevs_active[ar->pdev_idx]))
 		return -ENETDOWN;
 
 	reinit_completion(&ar->thermal.wmi_sync);
